  "methodology": {
    "detection_approach": "Multi-layered vulnerability detection combining authenticated AWS Inspector scans, unauthenticated external perimeter scans, OSV.dev vulnerability database, CISA KEV catalog, EPSS scoring, Bandit SAST analysis, continuous AWS Security Hub CSPM monitoring, and independent third-party penetration testing (most recently NetSPI, 2026-07-16). Detection is not limited to CVE-type vulnerabilities: cloud misconfigurations identified by automated control testing are tracked as vulnerabilities under FRR-VDR (VDR-CSO-DET). Pipeline version: vdr-cr26-v2026.09.13.02",
    "prioritization_framework": "CR26 (VER-EVA) contextual risk rating: Potential Agency Impact N-rating (N1-N5) per VER-EVA-EPA, informed by the VER-EVA-EFA factors \u2014 criticality and data sensitivity of affected resources, internet reachability (IRV), and exploitability (LEV) including penetration-test-confirmed exploitation and CISA KEV known-threat status. Per VER-EVA-AIA, exploitation is assumed automatable unless evidence proves otherwise.",
